\f2\b\fs30 \cf0 \strokec2 Balancing The Body
\f1\b0\fs24 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs30 \cf0 The thing I most want people to know - and that I hardly ever hear anyone talking about - is this simple message\'85
\f1\fs24 \

\f0\fs30 We\'92re in pain when some part of our body is working too hard. And the reason that part is working too hard is BECAUSE some other part isn\'92t working enough.\'a0
\f1\fs24 \

\f0\fs30 It really is that simple.\'a0
\f1\fs24 \

\f0\fs30 And this is especially true for chronic pain - particularly low back, hips, and shoulder pain.\'a0
\f1\fs24 \

\f0\fs30 The low back & hips along with the shoulders are the two main axles of the body. Everything else in the body depends upon the proper movement & alignment of these two main axles, just like in a car.
\f1\fs24 \

\f0\fs30 The axle connects one wheel on one side to another wheel on the other side. In your body, your hips & shoulders are balls in sockets - connecting opposite sides just like a car's axles connect its wheels.
\f1\fs24 \

\f0\fs30 These four key points - your two shoulders and two hips - create the foundation for your entire body's movement. If any one of these four points is off, it will set off a chain reaction throughout your entire system. When they're all aligned and functioning properly, the rest of your body will move with ease.
\f1\fs24 \

\f0\fs30 If those four points are sound then the rest of the body will have ease - and if they are off, then it throws the entire system into chaos
\f1\fs24 \

\f0\fs30 What is chaos?
\f1\fs24 \

\f0\fs30 Chaos is when a system breaks apart because it can no longer sustain itself at the level it\'92s at. So chaos is like leveling a building because it\'92s no longer functioning in a useful or desirable way. It has to change so that it can be rebuilt.
\f1\fs24 \

\f0\fs30 We need to let go of preconceived notions about exercise and various therapeutics so that our main focus can return to PROPER FUNCTION, soundness and balance. This must be our priority. Especially when we\'92re in pain.\'a0
\f1\fs24 \

\f0\fs30 That\'92s what The Amari Method offers.
\f1\fs24 \

\f0\fs30 A foundation built on strength and flexibility, rather than just one or the other.
